+This method extracts isosurfaces using OpenCL and OpenGL, employing a Histogram Pyramid (HP) to determine triangle counts and locations without atomic operations or sorting. It differs from sibling methods by replacing global atomics with a hierarchical reduction structure. It supports two paths: 3D textures (preferred) and buffers (fallback for NVIDIA GPUs lacking 3D texture write support). The HP uses type promotion (char -> short -> int) to prevent overflow.
 
 ### [GPU Marching Cubes with Atomic Counter Emission](4082-gpu-marching-cubes-with-atomic-counter-emission.md)
-A real-time isosurface meshing technique that uses one compute thread per grid cell. It classifies density, reserves vertex slots via atomic addition on indirect draw arguments, and writes vertices directly into a capped pool, avoiding prefix sums.
